From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alps Extended Images <noreply@cscs.ch>
Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: do not promote unused-variable to error on HIP

clang 23 emits an unused-variable warning inside ROCm 10's own
hip/amd_detail/amd_warp_sync_functions.h header (lastLane in
__warp_wave_bcast_permute). vLLM's HIP build adds
-Werror=unused-variable to every GPU target, so including that header
aborts the build. Keep the warning, drop the error promotion.
---
 cmake/utils.cmake | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/utils.cmake b/cmake/utils.cmake
--- a/cmake/utils.cmake
+++ b/cmake/utils.cmake
@@ -157,7 +157,6 @@
       "-DUSE_ROCM"
       "-DENABLE_FP8"
       "-U__HIP_NO_HALF_CONVERSIONS__"
       "-U__HIP_NO_HALF_OPERATORS__"
-      "-Werror=unused-variable"
       "-fno-gpu-rdc")
 
   endif()
